1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:09,842
Before a kitchen is cut, someone should read every label once. Ortiz kitchen: doors, drawers, a blind corner, a filler and end panels.

2
00:00:09,842 --> 00:00:18,755
Why bother? The label is what the person at the table has: if it’s wrong or unclear, the part gets banded wrong or lost on the cart.

3
00:00:18,755 --> 00:00:22,473
Labels PDF: one 100 x 70 mm label per part, in cut order, and each sheet starts with a header label.

4
00:00:22,473 --> 00:00:29,378
Header: sheet number, material and part count. Stick it on the stack so the sheet can be found again.

5
00:00:29,378 --> 00:00:39,046
A part label: part ID barcode, cabinet and part name, finished size, the edge diagram showing which edges are banded, and its sheet and order.

6
00:00:39,046 --> 00:00:48,256
Check the edge diagram against the cut list: a door is banded all round; a drawer front too. That is where mistakes cost a door.

7
00:00:48,256 --> 00:00:57,123
The odd parts deserve a look: drawer box parts, the blind panel, the filler and the end panels.

8
00:00:57,123 --> 00:01:07,486
Fillers and end panels go to install, not the assembly bench: their labels carry the same names as the room plan (F1, E1, E2), so the installer knows where each one goes. The filler adds: Scribe 1/2" on L2, trim to the wall.

9
00:01:07,486 --> 00:01:19,905
Sheet maps PDF: one page per sheet, every part at its spot with its number, and the machine origin. Labels go on as parts come off.

10
00:01:19,905 --> 00:01:33,936
Now an L-shaped corner, from the Novak kitchen: the L parts and the corner cleat have their own labels.

11
00:01:33,936 --> 00:01:43,138
The L bottom’s label draws the L, so the banded inside edges L3 and W3 are clear. A rectangle would hide which edges are inside.

12
00:01:43,138 --> 00:01:52,348
The cleat is marked "fix on site": it doesn’t go into the carcass at assembly, so it must not get lost in the offcut bin.

13
00:01:52,348 --> 00:01:57,936
Label printer? Labels ZPL sends the same labels to a Zebra printer. Same content, no PDF step.

14
00:01:57,936 --> 00:02:04,379
So: read the headers, the edge diagrams on show parts, and the odd parts once, before the first sheet goes on the machine.
